    {
      "label": "Gathering Hymn",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Gathering Hymn"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "St Aidan’s Day Hymn"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "text": "Glen Wesley · Tune: Battle Hymn of the Republic",
          "margin": "16px 0 22px"
        },
        {
          "type": "hymn",
          "verses": [
            [
              "We are walking in the footsteps",
              "of a gentle, pilgrim saint,",
              "who would meet you on the roadway",
              "with a blessing, not complaint,",
              "for the love of Christ is patient",
              "and it never will grow faint,",
              "and Aidan’s way goes on."
            ],
            [
              "Glory, glory, hallelujah!",
              "Glory, glory, hallelujah!",
              "Glory, glory, hallelujah!",
              "And Aidan’s way goes on."
            ],
            [
              "Every mind and every body",
              "is a bearer of the flame,",
              "every voice in every rhythm",
              "sings the glory of the Name,",
              "here at Aidan’s all are welcome,",
              "none excluded, none the same,",
              "for love goes walking on."
            ],
            [
              "Glory, glory, hallelujah!",
              "Glory, glory, hallelujah!",
              "Glory, glory, hallelujah!",
              "For love goes walking on."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Gathering",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Greeting"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "We are gathered in the name of the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit.",
          "response": "Amen."
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "The Lord be with you",
          "response": "And also with you"
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Welcome & Introduction"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer",
          "height": 10
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Introduction to the Feast"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Today we keep the feast of Aidan of Lindisfarne,",
            "the saint this parish is named for."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Aidan was an Irish monk, sent to Northumbria in 635",
            "after the mission before his gave up",
            "and went home calling the people stubborn."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Aidan said the people were not the problem.",
            "They had been given hard food too soon,",
            "and should have been led gently,",
            "at the pace they could go."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "So he walked, and stopped for whoever he met,",
            "and the church there grew from that."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "This parish took his name on purpose."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Call to Worship",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Call to Worship"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer",
          "height": 22
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "God did not come to us with force,",
            [
              "but with patience, and the offer of friendship.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Aidan walked the roads of Northumbria,",
            [
              "stopping to talk with whoever he met.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "He taught at the pace people could receive,",
            [
              "and made room for those a harsher teacher had lost.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "We gather as people still being taught,",
            [
              "still learning to speak the truth in love.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "margin": "0",
          "lines": [
            "Come, let us worship God,",
            [
              "who builds us up, one act of kindness at a time. Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Receiving God’s Mercy",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Receiving God’s Mercy"
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Invitation to Confession"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "In the spirit of St Aidan, take a moment.",
            "There is no hurry here.",
            "Bring whatever you are carrying, just as it is."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Aidan took the slow road on purpose,",
            "and the God he trusted is patient still."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Confession"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Loving God,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "we admit that we have done wrong:",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "in our thoughts, words, and actions.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Please forgive us.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Help us to change,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and guide us in the future.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Help us to live justly,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "to show mercy,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and to walk humbly with you.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Absolution"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "God, who is full of love and power,",
            "forgives you and sets you free.",
            "The Holy Spirit heals, strengthens, and guides you,",
            "so you may walk in new life in Christ."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "margin": "0",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Giving Praise",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Giving Praise"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer",
          "height": 22
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "We give thanks to you, God of the long road,",
            [
              "for you are patient with us,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and you do not give up.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "You called Aidan from Iona to a kingdom of strangers,",
            [
              "and he went on foot,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "so that no one would be passed by.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "You gave him nothing to command with,",
            [
              "only the gentleness that earns a hearing.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "He gave away what was given to him,",
            [
              "the king’s own horse,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "to a beggar on the road.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "From Lindisfarne you sent out teachers and healers,",
            [
              "and the body of Christ grew,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and was built up in love.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "We give you thanks and praise,",
            [
              "now and always. Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Prayer of the Day"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer",
          "height": 10
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "God of the slow road,",
            "you sent Aidan to people who had been given up on."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "margin": "0",
          "lines": [
            "Give us his patience,",
            "his trust in those who are not yet ready,",
            "and love enough to grow up together;",
            "through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
            [
              "Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Ephesians 4",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Bible and Teaching"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Readings"
        },
        {
          "type": "worktitle",
          "text": "Ephesians 4:11–16",
          "sub": "First reading"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "A reading from the letter of Paul to the Ephesians."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "paragraphs": [
            "He gave some apostles, some prophets, some evangelists, and some pastors and teachers. His purpose was to equip God’s people for the work of serving and building up the body of Christ until we all reach the unity of faith and knowledge of God’s Son. God’s goal is for us to become mature adults—to be fully grown, measured by the standard of the fullness of Christ. As a result, we aren’t supposed to be infants any longer who can be tossed and blown around by every wind that comes from teaching with deceitful scheming and the tricks people play to deliberately mislead others. Instead, by speaking the truth with love, let’s grow in every way into Christ, who is the head. The whole body grows from him, as it is joined and held together by all the supporting ligaments. The body makes itself grow in that it builds itself up with love as each one does its part."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "This is the word of the Lord",
          "response": "Thanks be to God",
          "margin": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Gospel",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Bible and Teaching"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Gospel"
        },
        {
          "type": "worktitle",
          "text": "Matthew 28:16–20"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            {
              "segments": [
                [
                  "Alleluia! ",
                  ""
                ],
                [
                  "Alleluia!",
                  "all"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "segments": [
                [
                  "Go and make disciples of all nations, says the Lord. ",
                  ""
                ],
                [
                  "Alleluia!",
                  "all"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "The Lord be with you",
          "response": "And also with you"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "A reading from the Good News according to Matthew.",
          "response": "Glory to you Lord Jesus Christ"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Now the eleven disciples went to Galilee, to the mountain where Jesus told them to go. When they saw him, they worshipped him, but some doubted. Jesus came near and spoke to them, “I’ve received all authority in heaven and on earth. Therefore, go and make disciples of all nations, baptising them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, teaching them to obey everything that I’ve commanded you. Look, I myself will be with you every day until the end of this present age.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "This is the good news of the Lord",
          "response": "Praise to you Lord Jesus Christ",
          "margin": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Sermon & Affirmation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Bible and Teaching"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Sermon"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Affirmation"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "We believe in God,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "maker of all,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "who raised Jesus to life",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and brings new life to the world.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "We believe in Christ,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "crucified and risen,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "alive forever—",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "calling us to justice, joy, and peace.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "We believe the Spirit is with us,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "opening hearts,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "renewing minds,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and breathing life into all creation.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "We believe the Church is Christ’s body—",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "diverse, united,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and welcoming all.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "We affirm the dignity of every person,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and are called to love without exception.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "margin": "0",
          "lines": [
            [
              "This is our faith,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "our hope,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "our joy.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Prayers & Peace",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Prayers and Peace"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Prayers of the People"
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Intercessions"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "text": "Led by the intercessor. Everyone responds to each petition with:"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "Lord in your mercy",
          "response": "Hear our prayer"
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Prayer for St Aidan’s"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "God of Mission,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "you call us to share your love.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Send your Holy Spirit to guide us",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "in deepening our discipleship,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "in welcoming everyone,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and in sharing your love with courage.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Help St Aidan’s grow",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "in faith, diversity,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and service to our community.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Conclusion to Prayers"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Loving God, you hear our prayers.",
            [
              "By your Spirit,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "guide us to live with open hearts,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "trusting in your presence",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and grace,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "through Jesus Christ our Lord. Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Greeting of Peace"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "We are the body of Christ",
          "response": "His Spirit is with us"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "The peace of the Lord be with you",
          "response": "And also with you",
          "margin": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Offertory Hymn",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Offertory Hymn"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Lift High The Cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "text": "TIS 351 · refrain, then verses 3, 4 & 5",
          "margin": "16px 0 22px"
        },
        {
          "type": "hymn",
          "verses": [
            [
              "Lift high the cross,",
              "the love of Christ proclaim",
              "till all the world adore",
              "his sacred name."
            ],
            [
              "All newborn servants",
              "of the Crucified",
              "bear on their brow the",
              "seal of him who died:",
              "Lift high the cross,",
              "the love of Christ proclaim",
              "till all the world adore",
              "his sacred name."
            ],
            [
              "From north and south, from",
              "east and west they raise",
              "in growing unison",
              "their song of praise:",
              "Lift high the cross,",
              "the love of Christ proclaim",
              "till all the world adore",
              "his sacred name."
            ],
            [
              "O Lord, once lifted",
              "on the glorious tree,",
              "draw all to you,",
              "let all the nations see:",
              "Lift high the cross,",
              "the love of Christ proclaim",
              "till all the world adore",
              "his sacred name."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Thanksgiving Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Holy Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Introduction to Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer",
          "height": 10
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Aidan kept a table where the poor were fed first,",
            "and gave away whatever was put into his hands."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Here is a table like that one.",
            "Nothing here is earned, and nothing here runs out.",
            "Everyone is welcome.",
            "Come as you are."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Sursum Corda"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "The Lord be with you.",
          "response": "And also with you"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "Lift up your hearts.",
          "response": "We lift them to the Lord."
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.",
          "response": "It is right to give our thanks and praise.",
          "margin": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Preface",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Holy Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Preface"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer",
          "height": 10
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "It is right to give you thanks,",
            "God of the patient and the persistent."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "From the beginning you made a world of good things,",
            [
              "and you taught us gently,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "feeding us with what we could receive.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "When we turned away, you did not abandon us.",
            [
              "You sent prophets who walked among the people,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and were known by their kindness before their words.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "In Jesus Christ you came the same way —",
            "on foot, unarmed, welcoming the doubters on the mountain,",
            [
              "and you gave yourself for the life of the world.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "You gave gifts to your church —",
            "apostles and prophets, evangelists, pastors and teachers,",
            [
              "so that all of us together might grow up into Christ.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "So with Aidan, and with all who have taught by kindness,",
            "we give you thanks and praise, saying together:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "margin": "0",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Blessed is our God,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "who teaches us gently and feeds us well.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Blessed is our God, forever.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Words of Institution",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Holy Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Words of Institution"
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Bread"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "On the night before he died,",
            "Jesus shared a meal with his friends.",
            "He took bread,",
            "gave thanks,",
            "broke it, and said:",
            "Take, eat.",
            "This is my body, given for you.",
            "Do this to remember me.",
            [
              "Lord my God.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Wine"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "margin": "0",
          "lines": [
            "After supper, he took the cup,",
            "gave thanks, and said:",
            "Drink this, all of you.",
            "This is my blood of the new covenant,",
            "poured out for you and for all,",
            "for the forgiveness of sin.",
            "Do this to remember me.",
            [
              "Lord my God.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Acclamation to Doxology",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Holy Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Acclamation"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Let us proclaim the mystery of faith."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Christ has died to set us free.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Christ is risen to make us whole.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Christ will come again with justice and joy.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Epiclesis"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Send your Spirit of life,",
            "that this bread and this cup",
            "may be for us the body and blood of Christ."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "As we eat and drink,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "renew your people in love,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "make us one body in Christ,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "our Saviour and Lord.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Doxology"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "With your Church across all of creation,",
            "we give you thanks and praise,",
            "joining the unending song:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "margin": "0",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Holy, holy, holy Lord,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "God of power and might,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Heaven and earth are full of your glory.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Praise to you in the highest.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Lord’s Prayer to Invitation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Holy Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "The Lord’s Prayer"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Father, uphold the holiness of your name.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Bring in your kingdom.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Give us the bread we need for today.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Forgive us our sins,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "for we also forgive everyone who has wronged us.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "And save us in times of trial.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "For you are worthy,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "our Lord and God,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "to receive glory and honour and power,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "because you created all things.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Breaking the Bread"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "This bread is broken,",
            "for Jesus gave himself for us.",
            [
              "In this act of love, we are made whole.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Invitation to Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "The gifts of God for the people of God."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "margin": "0",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Feed us, patient Christ,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "at the pace we are able to receive,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and make us gentle with one another",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "as you have been gentle with us.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Communion Anthem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Communion Anthem"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Jesus Christ, Be the Wine of Grace"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer"
        },
        {
          "type": "hymn",
          "verses": [
            [
              "In the singing, in the silence,",
              "in the hands expectant, open,",
              "in the blessing, in the breaking,",
              "in the presence at this table"
            ],
            [
              "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
              "be the wine of grace.",
              "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
              "be the bread of peace."
            ],
            [
              "In the question, in the answer,",
              "in the moment of acceptance,",
              "in the heart’s cry, in the healing,",
              "in the circle of your people."
            ],
            [
              "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
              "be the wine of grace.",
              "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
              "be the bread of peace."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Receiving Communion",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Receiving Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Speak O Lord"
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer"
        },
        {
          "type": "hymn",
          "verses": [
            [
              "Speak O Lord as we come to You",
              "To receive the food of Your holy word",
              "Take Your truth plant it deep in us",
              "Shape and fashion us in Your likeness",
              "That the light of Christ might be seen today",
              "In our acts of love and our deeds of faith",
              "Speak O Lord and fulfill in us",
              "All Your purposes for Your glory"
            ],
            [
              "Teach us Lord full obedience",
              "Holy reverence true humility",
              "Test our thoughts and our attitudes",
              "In the radiance of Your purity",
              "Cause our faith to rise,",
              "Cause our eyes to see",
              "Your majestic love and authority",
              "Words of power that can never fail",
              "Let their truth prevail over unbelief"
            ],
            [
              "Speak O Lord and renew our minds",
              "Help us grasp the heights of Your plans for us",
              "Truths unchanged from the dawn of time",
              "That will echo down through eternity",
              "And by grace we’ll stand on Your promises",
              "And by faith we’ll walk as You walk with us",
              "Speak O Lord till Your church is built",
              "And the earth is filled with Your glory"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "© 2005 Thankyou Music Ltd · CCLI 4615235"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Sending Out",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Sending Out God’s People"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Prayer after Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "Patient God,",
            "you have fed us at a table we did not earn.",
            "Send us out at walking pace,",
            "ready to stop for whoever we meet,",
            "and to give away what you have given us."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "h3",
          "text": "Gratitude for Communion"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            [
              "Lord,",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "we have broken your bread",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "and received your life.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "By the power of your Spirit",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "keep us always in your love",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
              "all"
            ],
            [
              "Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Notices",
          "margin": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Blessing & Dismissal",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Sending Out God’s People"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Blessing"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "The Lord be with you",
          "response": "And also with you"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "May God who is patient give you patience,",
            "Christ who walked the roads walk beside you,",
            "and the Spirit who gives gifts to the church",
            "build you up in love."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "lines": [
            "And the blessing of God —",
            "Father, Son, and Holy Spirit",
            "be with you and remain with you always.",
            [
              "Amen.",
              "all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "spacer"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Dismissal"
        },
        {
          "type": "versicle",
          "call": "Go in peace, to love and serve the Lord",
          "response": "In the name of Christ. Amen.",
          "margin": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Sending Hymn",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "eyebrow",
          "text": "Sending Hymn"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "God Gives Us A Future"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "text": "TIS 687",
          "margin": "16px 0 22px"
        },
        {
          "type": "hymn",
          "verses": [
            [
              "God gives us a future,",
              "daring us to go",
              "into dreams and dangers",
              "on a path unknown.",
              "We will face tomorrow",
              "in the Spirit’s power,",
              "we will let God change us,",
              "for new life starts now."
            ],
            [
              "We must leave behind us",
              "sins of yesterday,",
              "for God’s new beginning",
              "is a better way.",
              "Fear and doubt and habit",
              "must not hold us back:",
              "God gives hope, and insight,",
              "and the strength we lack."
            ],
            [
              "Holy Spirit, teach us",
              "how to read the signs,",
              "how to meet the challenge",
              "of our troubled times.",
              "Love us into action,",
              "stir us into prayer,",
              "till we choose God’s life,",
              "and find our future there."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}